      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The effectiveness of economic sanctions is a highly debated topic in international relations. Proponents argue they can exert diplomatic pressure to promote human rights or democratic change by imposing costs on target regimes. Conversely, critics contend that sanctions often harm the general population disproportionately, and can be used as a form of economic coercion by powerful states against weaker ones. Ultimately, whether they are a tool for reform or bullying often depends on the specific context and execution of the sanctions.",
      "source": "target",
